      "side": 1,
      "message": "I was reading the code again and looks like the effect of these two events is basically setting `vcpu-\u003earch.mp_state` to `KVM_MP_STATE_INIT_RECEIVED` (and vcpu_reset hypercall) and then to `KVM_MP_STATE_RUNNABLE` (and sipi_deliver hypercall). So, I was wondering if we set this directly here to `KVM_MP_STATE_RUNNABLE`, would we be able to save couple of hypercalls? WDYT?",
